      "detailEn": "Kalepark (originally called Leonkastron; and later Güzelhisar, meaning \"Beautiful Castle\" in Turkish) was procured and further fortified by Genoese merchants as a medieval fortress on the east side of Trabzon, Turkey. The fortress was built on a rocky outcrop strategically overlooking both harbors of the city: the summer harbor at a distance to the west, and the winter harbor just to the east of it."
